IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Writ Petition (Civil) No. 118 of 2016
CITATION: (2017) 9 SCC 1
YEAR: 2017

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: J.S. Khehar, Kurian Joseph, R.F. Nariman, U.U. Lalit, S. Abdul Nazeer

PARTIES:
Shayara Bano vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Muslim Personal Law (Shariat) Application Act, 1937, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 14, Article 21, Article 25

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
triple talaq unconstitutional, talaq-e-biddat, manifest arbitrariness doctrine

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

By a 3:2 majority, held instantaneous Triple Talaq (Talaq-e-Biddat) void and unconstitutional, establishing the doctrine of manifest arbitrariness under Article 14.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 14, Article 21, Article 25.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

